    {
      "id": "Hbol",
      "code_hash": "fd6452b0fa73eaeb03023d0c61aaa021",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/html": "<div style='display: flex;flex: 1;flex-direction: column;justify-content: flex-start;align-items: normal;flex-wrap: nowrap;gap: 0.5rem'><span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h1 id=\"live-coding-music-in-python\">\ud83c\udf00 Live-coding music in Python</h1>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Live coding</strong> is making music by writing code while it plays. Here is what that\nlooks like: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@Switch-Angel\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Switch Angel</a> builds a deep acid\ntrack from scratch in two minutes, in <a href=\"https://strudel.cc\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Strudel</a>, the\nJavaScript sibling of the patterns you'll write below.</span></span><iframe src='https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/HkgV_-nJOuE' title='2 Minute Deep Acid in Strudel (from scratch), by Switch Angel' style='display:block;width:100%;max-width:720px;aspect-ratio:16/9;border:0;border-radius:12px' allow='accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture' allowfullscreen></iframe><span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\"><a href=\"https://ktaletsk.github.io/tidaleddy/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">eddy</a> brings the same pattern language,\nfrom <a href=\"https://tidalcycles.org\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">TidalCycles</a>, to Python. You write short patterns of\nrhythm and melody, and eddy turns them into sound, synthesized right here in the\nnotebook with numpy.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">This notebook starts with a few small sounds, then shows what Python adds: patterns\nbuilt by code, by a cellular automaton, by your words, and by a loop you bend\nwith the mouse.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>In every box below:</strong> press <strong>\u25b6 Play</strong>, click the code to change it (<strong>\u21b5</strong> applies),\ndrag the blue numbers, and click sound names to cycle through them. Changes come in on\nthe next loop, without stopping the music. <strong>\u25a0 Hush</strong> stops.</span></span></div>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
